Verdant Holdings was an agricultural powerhouse, focused on high-density, high-yield crops that could keep pace with a ballooning population. Its compound aboard the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]] held two camps of tents and makeshift greenhouses, split by a feud between the half-giant who led one side and an elf who spoke with as much authority on the other. The half-giant's people leaned toward the [[Org/RunGunners/index|RunGunners]].

Its leadership had been in question for some time. The company's head was killed, and it was choosing a new one from within; [[Org/Verdant Holdings/People/Dr. Thrain|Dr. Thrain]] spoke for it in the meantime, and kept a grudge against the [[Org/Hildebrandt Corporation/index|Hildebrandt Corporation]] over an old scuffle.

At an All Hallows Eve party among the guests some months ago, a group from Verdant came in disguised as some of the hosts, took a number of them hostage, poured acid across the floors, and broke into a vault at the middle of the city. They were stopped. The company afterward offered the Party a conditional alliance; the Party, hearing this account, kept its distance.

On the night of the second tithe the whole compound was destroyed. Where both camps stood is a single crater in the ground, its shape and the absence of any debris marking it as the work of ordnance planted on the company's Heart and set off so that the ruin looked like a failure to pay the tithe. Everyone in the compound died with it.
